AmiSurf - third-party components and licences
=======================================================
AmiSurf itself is (c) 2026 Rich. Licence texts are in the LICENSES
drawer next to this file (and in Host/LICENSES/ in the AmiKit edition).

Pages are rendered by Chrome, Chromium or Firefox on a Linux PC (asb-chromed);
the Amiga program is a thin client.

Amiga program (AmiSurf, -020, -gadtools)
* stb_image (Sean Barrett) - PNG/JPEG decoding of frames.
    Public domain / MIT (dual).  LICENSES/stb_image.txt
* QOI - The Quite OK Image format (Dominic Szablewski) - frame tiles.
    MIT.  LICENSES/qoi-MIT.txt
* Built against the MUI developer headers; MUI itself is installed by the user
  and not included.
* Ken's Icons - Kenneth's DualPNG Workbench icons (the AmiSurf drawer
  icon), also shipped in AmiKit. Copied byte-for-byte, never re-saved.
* Toolbar icon shapes: Lucide - ISC licence, Copyright (c) Lucide Contributors.
  https://lucide.dev
* ReadMe/CHANGES/ATTRIBUTIONS/LICENSES icons: the AmiStudio suite's shared
  classic OS3 ReadMe icon (as in AmiStudio Paint).

Linux engine (asb-chromed; host tarball and the AmiKit edition's Host/)
* stb_image and QOI, as above.
* OpenSSL 3 libcrypto (statically linked) - Apache License 2.0.
    LICENSES/OpenSSL-Apache-2.0.txt
* zlib (Jean-loup Gailly, Mark Adler) and Zstandard (Meta), statically linked
  as part of libcrypto - zlib licence / BSD-3-Clause.
    LICENSES/zlib.txt, LICENSES/zstd-BSD-3-Clause.txt

